          tesseract-ocr,
          vpx-tools,
Description: sparc lab of wsh-pve: unattended guest installs into Proxmox VE VMs
 The lab of the wsh-pve project drives a guest's serial console and framebuffer
 the way a person would and records every step. Its main command installs a
 named target (Solaris 2.6 on a SPARCstation 5 or 20, so far) into a new VM on
 a Proxmox VE node, from install media the user provides, and leaves a powered
 off VM with known, publicly documented login details.
 .
 Commands: wsh-lab (install, targets, media, run, serve, ...) and wsh-lab-mcp,
 an MCP server that lets an AI assistant see and type on an allowed VM. The MCP
 server's Python SDK is not packaged in Debian: wsh-lab-mcp --setup installs it
 into a venv under /var/lib/wsh-lab from the pinned, hash-checked requirements
 in this package.
 .
 The package works with whatever qemu-server is installed and depends on none
 of the wsh-pve packages. tesseract-ocr is needed for targets driven on a
 framebuffer, vpx-tools for the framebuffer videos of a run.
